- Environment files define the runtime configuration of Oracle EBS.

- They contain environment variables such as ORACLE_HOME, APPL_TOP, and database connection details.

- These files must be sourced before running any EBS commands.

- There are two main types:
  - APPSORA.env (legacy environment file)
  - <CONTEXT_NAME>.env (AutoConfig-generated, instance-specific)

- The context-based environment file is the recommended approach in modern EBS systems.

- Using the wrong environment file may result in connecting to the wrong database or executing incorrect operations.
